# {{idiom}} After a very long time; [[eventually]]; over a long period of time; more generally.
#:''It may cost a bit more up front, but I think you will find that it is a sturdier product '''in the long run'''.''
#:''If we have learned one thing from the history of invention and discovery, it is that, '''in the long run''' — and often in the short one — the most daring prophecies seem laughably conservative.'' - [[q: Arthur C. Clarke| Arthur C. Clarke]]
